e sense of increasing contact with reality, is a logically necessary part. In the biological and social sciences this becomes even more evident. ....\" [from back cover]."},"note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"by Michael Polanyi."},{"@type":"bibliography","#text":"Includes bibliographical references and index."}],"subject":[{"@authority":"ram","topic":"Théorie de la connaissance"},{"@authority":"ram","topic":"Philosophie des sciences"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":["Science","Philosophy"]},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Knowledge, Theory of"},{"@authority":"mesh","topic":"Knowledge"},{"@authority":"mesh","topic":"Philosophy"},{"@authority":"mesh","topic":"Science"},{"@authority":"mesh","topic":"Mental Processes"}],"classification":[{"@authority":"lcc","#text":"Q175 .P82 1962"},{"@authority":"nlm","#text":"B 945 .P584 P467 1962"}],"identifier":[{"@type":"isbn","#text":"0226672883"},{"@type":"isbn","#text":"0226672875"},{"@type":"lccn","@invalid":"yes","#text":"^^^58005162^"},{"@type":"oclc","#text":"3259137"}],"relatedItem":{"@otherType":"HOLLIS record","location":{"url":"https://id.lib.harvard.edu/alma/990004041500203941/catalog"}},"location":[{"physicalLocation":{"@displayLabel":"Harvard repository","@type":"repository","@valueURI":"http://isni.org/isni/0000000463633307","#text":"Lamont Library, Harvard University"},"shelfLocator":"Q175 .P82x 1962"},{"physicalLocation":{"@displayLabel":"Harvard repository","@type":"repository","@valueURI":"http://isni.org/isni/0000000121705139","#text":"Harvard Divinity School Library, Harvard University"},"shelfLocator":"  Q175     .P82 1962  "},{"physicalLocation":{"@displayLabel":"Harvard repository","@type":"repository","@valueURI":"http://isni.org/isni/000000046073724X","#text":"Cabot Science Library, Harvard University"},"shelfLocator":"Q175 .P82 1962"},{"physicalLocation":{"@displayLabel":"Harvard repository","@type":"repository","@valueURI":"http://isni.org/isni/000000046073724X","#text":"Cabot Science Lib